.TH OFUMO 1 "September 2026" "ofumo 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ofumo \- Koishi Fumo desktop pet with oneko-compatible controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ofumo
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OFumo displays a shaped Koishi Fumo which follows the pointer using movement
and idle-state semantics derived from classic oneko.
.PP
On X11, pointer and window information is obtained directly through Xlib. On
KDE Plasma Wayland, OFumo draws through XWayland but obtains the global cursor
and active-window geometry from KWin using a temporary helper bridge.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -help ", " -h ", " --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.BI -display " DISPLAY"
Use the specified X display.
.TP
.BI -fg " COLOR"
Set foreground color.
.TP
.BI -bg " COLOR"
Set background color.
.TP
.BI -speed " N"
Pixels moved per timer tick. Default: 13.
.TP
.BI -time " US"
Update interval in microseconds. Default: 125000.
.TP
.BI -idle " N"
Pointer movement threshold needed to wake the pet. Default: 6.
.TP
.BI -name " NAME"
Set the OFumo X11 window name.
.TP
.B -towindow
Select an X11/XWayland window and chase it.
.TP
.BI -toname " NAME"
Chase an X11/XWayland window by its X11 title.
.TP
.B -tofocus
Run to/on top of the focused window. On KDE Wayland, KWin supplies native
Wayland active-window geometry.
.TP
.BI -position " GEOMETRY"
Offset the target position relative to the pointer or target window.
.TP
.B -rv
Swap foreground and background colors.
.TP
.B -noshape
Do not use the X SHAPE extension. The OFumo window is rectangular.
.TP
.B -debug
Use synchronous X11 requests for debugging.
.TP
.B -patchlevel
Print the OFumo version and exit.
.TP
.BI -cursor " N"
Set X cursor-font glyph N on the X root window while cleaning up. This is an
X11/XWayland facility and does not control the native Wayland cursor.
.TP
.BR -neko ", " -tora ", " -dog ", " -bsd_daemon ", " -sakura ", " -tomoyo
Accepted for command-line compatibility with oneko. Koishi is currently the
only OFumo character, so these flags do not yet change the sprite.
.TP
.BI --backend " MODE"
OFumo extension. Select pointer backend: auto, x11, or kwin. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
OFumo extension. Print backend and state diagnostics.
.TP
.B --version
OFumo extension. Print the version and exit.
.SH WAYLAND NOTES
OFumo selects the backend at startup. X11 sessions use the direct Xlib path.
KDE Plasma Wayland sessions use KWin for global cursor and active-window state
while the shaped pet window is still rendered through XWayland.
.PP
Other Wayland compositors are not supported in version 0.0.1.
.PP
On KDE Plasma Wayland, -towindow and -toname still use X11 selection/title
lookup and can therefore target X11/XWayland windows only.

.SH ANIMATIONS
Koishi uses directional, sleep, wink, disappearance, spawn, click and spin
frames. Ambient winks are intentionally infrequent. The spin special cycles
left, back, right and front twice and may occur as a random idle fidget.

.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Fridman (Schermaiolo).
.SH SEE ALSO
oneko(6)
